      "content": "You are right to point to the strong perception of political bias in the use of these powerful tools, and that \"unintended harm to the populace\" is a major critique in the literature.\n\nSkeptics argue that the \"liberal interventionism\" inherent in some sanction policies often prioritizes the political agenda of the powerful states over the well-being of the targeted, often more vulnerable, global political systems.\n\nThis perspective strongly suggests that the *political power behind the sanction, more than the sanction itself, is the real decisive factor in its outcome in the real world of great power politics",
